      48,
      150
    ],
    "span_decades_at_max": 2.221,
    "span_decades_at_median": 1.9103,
    "span_decades_note": "MEASURED over all 321,123 LB fragments: median 244 bp (1.9103 decades), p99 308 bp (2.011), max 499 bp (2.2210). Only 4.0% of rows reach 300 bp and 0.015% reach 400 bp. Against the measured tile sibling's 1.70 decades the honest gain is +0.21 at the MEDIAN (244/150 = 1.63x more length), NOT the +0.52 / 3.33x the maximum suggests. Quote the median figure; the max describes 49 fragments.",
    "leakage_unit": "contiguous genomic block, start // 50000",
    "length_rule": "zero-pad to 499 with MASKED pooling; padded positions excluded",
    "verdicts": {
      "PYRAMID_ADDS": "gain >= margin AND >= min_seeds_winning seeds win -- a reproducible lift",
      "WEAK_PYRAMID": "gain > 0 AND >= min_seeds_winning seeds win, but below the margin -- a REPRODUCIBLE gain that fell short of the effect-size bar",
      "INDETERMINATE_GAIN_NOT_REPRODUCIBLE": "gain > 0 but FEWER than min_seeds_winning seeds win -- a positive gain that did NOT reproduce, which is neither a measured lift nor a measured negative and must not be read as either",
      "NO_GAIN": "gain <= 0 -- the pyramid does not beat the length-invariant default",
      "INVALID_NULL_SCORED": "the shuffled-label control scored; nothing may be graded",
      "INVALID_PAD_LEAKED": "padding changed a score; the masked-pooling premise is broken"
    },
    "validity_controls": {
      "shuffled_labels": "AMENDED 2026-10-27, BEFORE any scored run, because the first design was MEASURED invalid. It was: one seed, |rho| < 0.05. The null's own spread makes that unusable -- measured over 5 seeds at N=4,000 the null is median -0.0008 / mean +0.0130 / **sd 0.1016**, range -0.1236..+0.1301, so a single-seed 0.05 bar FAILS 3 of 5 times on a pipeline that is demonstrably centred on zero. The first smoke duly returned a FALSE INVALID_NULL_SCORED. WHY the spread is that large, and it is not a defect: early stopping trips almost immediately once the train-side labels are permuted, leaving weights near initialisation, so the model is close to a RANDOM linear functional of base composition -- and composition predicts expression on this rung at spearman(GC, expression) = -0.1169, which is the same magnitude as the whole kmer4 comparator (0.1120). A random composition-like feature therefore lands anywhere in +/-0.13 by chance. NOW: the null runs on ALL seeds and the bar is on the MEDIAN, |median| < margin (0.02); the per-seed values and the sd are both reported so a reader can see the power. **The primary noise control was already pre-registered and is the SEED-COUNT bar**: under a null centred on zero each seed wins with p=0.5, so >= 8 of 10 has p = 0.0547. The single-seed null bar was both redundant and miscalibrated.",
      "null_median_bar": 0.02,
      "pad_invariance": "a sequence must score identically whatever length it is padded to",
      "length_matched_subset": "AMENDED 2026-10-27 from >= 400 bp to >= 300 bp, BEFORE any encoder number existed. The 400 bp threshold was frozen without measuring the distribution and selects 49 of 321,123 rows (0.015%) -- a control too small to falsify anything, which is worse than no control because it LOOKS like one. 300 bp selects 12,896 rows (4.0%) and is powered. Still the minority of the substrate, so it is a padding check, NOT a second headline. If the headline and this subset disagree in SIGN, padding is implicated and the headline is WITHDRAWN rather than explained.",
      "length_matched_threshold_bp": 300
    },
    "predicted_outcome": "NO_GAIN or WEAK_PYRAMID",
    "prediction_rationale": "Recorded BEFORE the run. Four reasons a negative is expected: (a) the conv encoder already failed to beat a SINGLE GC NUMBER on the easier tile rung (+0.0122, paired CI includes zero); (b) `load_fragments`' own docstring argues k-mer features are the honest default here precisely BECAUSE they are length-invariant, which is the property a fixed-window conv lacks; (c) this rung's best measured arm reaches only 0.1313 of a 0.7928 ceiling (16.6%), so the recoverable signal looks thin for every model class, not just this one; (d) more SPAN is only useful if regulatory signal actually lives above 150 bp, which is the hypothesis under test and not an assumption in its favour.",
    "negative_scope": "A negative here means: a 4-scale conv pyramid over zero-padded, masked-pooled fragments, trained under the registered protocol on block-split LB fragments, did not beat 4-mer counts + ridge by 0.02 Spearman. It would NOT mean sequence context above 150 bp is uninformative, NOT that multi-resolution modelling fails in general, and NOT anything about the tile rung, which has a different ceiling and a different incumbent.",
    "revival_condition": "a length-invariant architecture (dilated conv, attention with length masking) or a rung whose fragments are long enough that padding is negligible across the whole set."
